  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1628.01 Railway Shipments",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1628.01 Railway Shipments.\n\n(a) Shipments of explosives by trailer-on-flatcar or container-on-flatcar shall not be unloaded at a non-carrier's station unless the consignee is there to receive them or, unless properly locked and secure, storage facilities are provided at that point for their protection. If delivery cannot be made, the shipment shall be taken to the next or nearest carrier's station for delivery.\n\n(b) For shipment of high explosives, when practicable at any point, the carrier shall assign regular days for receiving trailers and containers for shipment.\n\n(c) To enable the carrier to provide proper flatcars for shipment of high explosives, the shipper shall give to the carrier not less than 24 hours notice of his or her intention to offer such shipments and state their destinations. When a regular day has been appointed to receive trailers and containers for shipment, this notice may be waived by the carrier, but the explosives shipment shall be delivered on such days in time to permit proper inspection, billing, and loading on that day.\n\nSource. #2220, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2837, eff 8-27-84; ss by #4584, eff 3-3-89; ss by #5996, INTERIM, eff 3-3-95, EXPIRES, 7-1-95; ss by #6054, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03\n\nNew. #8116, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRES: 1-10-05; ss by #8231, eff 12-20-04; ss by #10396, eff 8-15-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1600.html"
